  "assessments": [
    "Kestrel-only Server package remains independent; every Database composition requires Rust ORM/driver/pool/transaction engine, C# syntax/DTO only. No product managed DB fallback.",
    "SeaORM model Engine is one native module with generated static models; new schema requires controlled native build and source generators never invoke Cargo.",
    "Credit precedes allocation, copy double-credit, waiter bounds, no-return-before-owner-release and shutdown/quiescence are explicit; finite model does not prove RSS or real scheduler liveness.",
    "MCP 2026-07-28 and 2025-11-25 profiles are separated; annotated generic reflection is not mislabeled zero-reflection; upstream rooted net10 AOT fixture is not product net11 proof.",
    "PG next-statement ReadCommitted snapshot requirement, Unknown semantics, protected idempotent recovery, outbox at-least-once and durable-blob-before-reference are explicit.",
    "C#/Rust examples are uncompiled, Python SQLite response loss is simulated after real COMMIT, precommit process exit is real but not OS power loss.",
    "Explicit DataSession.CloseAsync(deadline) releases HTTP waiting only; Pending retains parent leases/roots/budget, preserves Unknown, does not capture request scope or introduce extra await-using join. Actual C#/Rust behavior is B21/B22 verification, not proved by SQLite prototype."
  ],
